# Three displacement ranks for actual common-image lifts

Conjugation carries each of the three common-image first-class lift fibers
to the original x-fiber. Only masks 96, 195 and 768 are needed for the
intrinsic central involution: the first has pair rank sixteen with x,
and the other two have rank twenty. The matrices, products and two-way
row expansions below are checked by the kernel in the original ATLAS basis.
Source: Kleidman--Wilson (1988), Section 2.1, p.489, and the native ATLAS
representation documented in `Janko4.Model.Data`.
-/
